20G\u001b[38;5;105m(total_cents + divisor // 2) // divisor\u001b[39m instead of\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bfloor division. This makes tax calculations correct: 7% of 1050\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bcents\u001b[12G= 73.5 cents →\u001b[27G74 cen\u001b[34Gs.\u001b[37G\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B2.\u001b[6G\u001b[38;5;105m\u001b[1mapp/split.py\u001b[22m\u001b[39m: Updated \u001b[38;5;105msplit_bill()\u001b[41G\u001b[39mto\u001b[44Guse\u001b[48Gfloor\u001b[54Gdivision\u001b[63Gdirectly\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  \u001b[6Ginstead of calling \u001b[38;5;105mdiv_cen\u001b[33Gs()\u001b[39m. Bill splitting must use floor\u001b[K\u001b[30;1H\u001b[28;3H\u001b[?25h"]
